WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:04.230
Let's go next to our caller from the 8 5 8
area code, who's calling today from 8 5 8.

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.160
Yes, I mean, yes, it is.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.360
Hi, it's Matthew from Southern California.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:12.960
Hey, Matthew, it's a.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:18.369
Oh, well, I mean, I had a main question, but
I wanted to make a quick comment.

00:00:18.369 --> 00:00:22.519
I don't know if you know L.A. and San Diego.

00:00:22.519 --> 00:00:27.189
I don't know if they're the exact same, ORDINATE
says, but they were closing all the beaches

00:00:27.189 --> 00:00:33.820
and all of the trails because so many people
were looking for outdoor activity to keep

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:36.350
their minds off of everything.

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:39.239
Yeah, they just couldn't keep their distance.

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:42.320
I didn't know that my brother lives in Southern
California.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:46.969
And obviously, he told me about the stay home
order that started and all of that.

00:00:46.969 --> 00:00:47.969
But I did.

00:00:47.969 --> 00:00:49.370
I knew a lot of people were going to trails.

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:51.770
I didn't know that they were starting to be
closed down.

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:55.380
That that's it's unfortunate because one of
the things that seems like a good idea is

00:00:55.380 --> 00:01:00.449
if you keep your distance outside, you know,
get the vitamin D, get the exercise, etc.

00:01:00.449 --> 00:01:03.190
But if people are just crowding, it defeats
the purpose.

00:01:03.190 --> 00:01:04.739
Oh, definitely.

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:09.509
So it's unfortunate, but seems it seems necessary.

00:01:09.509 --> 00:01:10.509
Yeah.

00:01:10.509 --> 00:01:12.700
My main question was about the talk.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:17.920
I hear a little less of it now, but when there
was talk about back during some of the most

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:21.780
recent primaries, there was actually talk
about the general election as well.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:29.380
And it was about, you know, how do we deal
with this virus while having voting access

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:34.590
or is it possible that Trump would try to
delay the election or something?

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:40.860
And I'm thinking maybe we should be reframing
it to voter access, you know, vote by mail

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:48.759
or everybody automatically gets a ballot like
California's system is slow, but we get like

00:01:48.759 --> 00:01:49.759
everyone.

00:01:49.759 --> 00:01:51.810
It depends on the county.

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:54.119
They're trying to get everyone to get a similar
model.

00:01:54.119 --> 00:01:59.070
But yeah, generally speaking, especially if
you register ahead of time, it's mailed to

00:01:59.070 --> 00:02:01.159
you have like 11 days to vote.

00:02:01.159 --> 00:02:06.390
And if you're a last minute voter haze, you
still get to wait till the last day to decide.

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:11.610
And then you have you at least in L.A. this
specific year, you could bring it to any voting

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:12.610
center.

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:14.490
But most people didn't know that that was
the change.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:15.910
So then there were still long lines.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:21.260
But if everyone was on board with that kind
of system, you could just mail it or drop

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:23.820
it off somewhere and everyone would have theirs
at home.

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:24.820
So absolutely.

00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:25.820
I don't know.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:29.860
Maybe there's a way lately that I've always
really been warning people, if you are counting

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:35.310
on thinking of or expecting that the November
election will be delayed.

00:02:35.310 --> 00:02:39.390
It's not going to be I can't think of any
way that that would really happen.

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:42.621
And remember, on the tail end of it, I don't
think that it shouldn't.

00:02:42.621 --> 00:02:45.980
And if it didn't happen, eventually Nancy
Pelosi becomes president and there's no way

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:48.010
Trump would allow that to happen.

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:53.730
So the question is, can we get a system in
place that makes more sense where people can

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:54.730
vote remotely?

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:57.370
Unfortunately, I doubt that that's going to
happen.

00:02:57.370 --> 00:03:03.510
And I think ultimately what this will be is
a battle of who how bad is the pandemic situation

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:07.140
at the time, who's willing to go out and who's
not?

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:12.010
And how do you value the risk of contracting
it versus your desire to cast a ballot in

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:13.010
November?

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:14.710
I think ultimately it's going to be as simple
as that.

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:19.760
And, you know, the new vote by mail systems
in states that don't have them postponements,

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:21.450
I don't think any of it's going to happen.

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:26.760
It's going to be who's actually going to say,
I want to vote enough that I will risk getting

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:32.260
the corona virus depending on how prevalent
it still is in November?

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:38.690
Do you think it's possible maybe just a couple
of states will change their laws beforehand,

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:41.670
maybe, maybe better, maybe they must.

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:44.150
I guess it just depends on the individual
state politics.

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:50.330
I'm guessing there's no real clear path on
the federal level to try to facilitate that.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.330
There isn't.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:56.000
And I think if states want to put it in place,
a system like that that don't already have

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:00.170
that system, if they don't start working on
that in the next four to six weeks, I think

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:05.140
it's just not going to happen because these
things take a very long time.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:06.140
So depressing.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:07.140
Thanks.

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:08.140
All right, appreciate the call.

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:08.870
Thank you

